            "review_title": "Review at San Dining",
            "review_text": "sales@greencanaltravel.com\nMelbourne, Australia7 contributions\n0\nExcellent cooking course\nDec 2024 • Family\nOur family had an impressive holiday in Vietnam. We came to Saigon, which was alive and had a warm, sunny and hot climate. When we came to Hanoi, the atmosphere was completely different: It was cold, the streets were full, but compared to Saigon it was quieter. We stayed at the San Grand Hotel, a great hotel near Hoan Kiem Lake. We enjoyed excellent breakfasts at the San Dining restaurant and learned how to prepare some popular but very delicious Vietnamese dishes in a cooking class led by the San Dining chefs. They led us to the market where the food was very cheap and fresh. I am proud that I prepared Hanoi-style spring rolls myself. Our three daughters were very happy that they made egg coffee themselves and learned to roll spring rolls that they like to eat. Many thanks to the chefs and staff of San Dining who helped us with food shopping that day. Unforgettable memories – now we can prepare Vietnamese food at home.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from German\nShow original\nWritten January 11, 2025",
